ed film  pictures and words that would go on to  be famous for nearly a century  this new evidence told a compelling  story two criminals in love fighting  against the world police quickly slapped  their photos on the couple's wanted  posters in the hopes that more people  will recognize them but that only made  them more famous than ever  suddenly the image of clyde being a  ruthless gang leader and bonnie as a  cigar-smoking gun-wielding sidekick was  front-page news and people loved it it  was cool and sexy and totally different  from most people's reality during the  great depression even if they were  committing crimes and killing people  america was entertained bonnie and clyde  were the great depressions robin hood  figures stealing money from the man  giving the system the middle finger  although they never gave any money back  to the poor but for bonnie and clyde the  high was never meant to last  [Music]  bonnie and clyde didn't mind killing  people if they had to but they didn't  like murdering just for the sake of it  it was more like if they didn't shoot  their way out they would end up in jail  or dead  and that just wasn't an option  but they weren't naive to the reality  that their spree was unsustainable long  term quite the opposite in fact in one  of her poems bonnie wrote quote they  don't think they're too smart or  desperate they know the law always wins  they've been shot at before but they do  not ignore that death is the wages of  sin end quote  quote someday they'll go down together  and they'll bury them side by side to a  few it'll be grief to the law a relief  but it's death for bonnie and clyde end  quote it was like she had a glimpse into  the future  the only thing bonnie got wrong was that  they weren't buried together against  their wishes on that fateful day when  the couple was ambushed on their way to  their friend's house when everyone  pushed and shoved to get a glimpse of  their corpses they were surprised they  didn't see two